,{"raise":0,"reaffirm":0,"cut":0}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":-0.0092,"r5":0.0813,"r1_spy":-0.0258,"r5_spy":0.0872}}],"quotes":[{"c":"NYT 2018 Q3","e":"nyt","d":"2018-11-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland Caputo","x":"…which is the commercial printing, which as you know, includes both the cost of newsprint which we passed through to the client and the cost of our people in the production center, but also we've got cost that fall into the production lines that are in news and editorial, so that's continuing the…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/01/new-york-times-co-nyt-q3-2018-earnings-conference.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2018 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2019-02-06","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Mark Thompson","x":"So cable and digital operator at FX and Hulu over-the-top streaming service.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/07/the-new-york-times-nyt-q4-2018-earnings-conference.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2018 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2019-02-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Meredith Levien","x":"I think it's worth noting that we have not raised prices in digital in seven and a half years since the launch of the model.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/07/the-new-york-times-nyt-q4-2018-earnings-conference.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2018 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2019-02-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Craig Huber","x":"Maybe if we could start, you mentioned early on, if I heard you're right, about the price increase for the digital-only subs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/07/the-new-york-times-nyt-q4-2018-earnings-conference.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q1","e":"nyt","d":"2019-05-08","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Meredith Kopit Levien","x":"I'll also say on Crosswords, we launched our first what I would call middle funnel, so not just direct to consumer marketing effort in Crosswords I think late in Q4, early Q1, and that's been really generative for the business and modest as far as expenditures, so I'm excited about that.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/08/new-york-times-co-nyt-q1-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q1","e":"nyt","d":"2019-05-08","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"This decline was partially offset by a home delivery price increase that began early in the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/08/new-york-times-co-nyt-q1-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q2","e":"nyt","d":"2019-08-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Mark Thompson","x":"These partnerships are distinctive and difficult to replicate and give us real pricing power.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/07/new-york-times-co-nyt-q2-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q2","e":"nyt","d":"2019-08-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"This decrease in print subscription revenues was partially offset by a home delivery price increase that was implemented early in the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/07/new-york-times-co-nyt-q2-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q2","e":"nyt","d":"2019-08-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark Thompson","x":"We think many news organizations, have somehow tried to [Indecipherable] go things through cost cutting and reducing their newsrooms.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/07/new-york-times-co-nyt-q2-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q2","e":"nyt","d":"2019-08-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Craig Anthony Huber","x":"Given the ongoing demise of the smaller and mid-size newspapers out there and you've the announcement of Gannett and New Media merging, talking about $300 million of cost cutting.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/07/new-york-times-co-nyt-q2-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q3","e":"nyt","d":"2019-11-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A Caputo","x":"This decrease in print subscription revenues was partially offset by a home delivery price increase that was implemented early in the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/06/new-york-times-co-nyt-q3-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q3","e":"nyt","d":"2019-11-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A Caputo","x":"And also as Mark mentioned we are planning a rollout of a price increase to tenured subscribers sometime in 2020 and that will also take some pressure off ARPU.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/06/new-york-times-co-nyt-q3-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q3","e":"nyt","d":"2019-11-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Roland A Caputo","x":"We recorded two special items in the quarter a $4 million charge related to our restructuring and a $2 million gain from a multi-employer pension plan liability adjustment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/06/new-york-times-co-nyt-q3-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2020-02-06","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Mark Thompson","x":"We're beginning to learn from others including some of the big streamers about trying to fit introductory prices to different markets around the world.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/06/new-york-times-co-nyt-q4-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2020-02-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"As was mentioned in this quarter, we have begun to phase in a price increase for many of our more tenured digital new subscriptions, with those currently paying $15 per billing cycle moving to $17.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/06/new-york-times-co-nyt-q4-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2019 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2020-02-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"The effect on Q1 digital subscription revenue from this price increase is expected to be modest due to the rollout occurring late in the quarter and this is reflected in our guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/06/new-york-times-co-nyt-q4-2019-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q1","e":"nyt","d":"2020-05-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"…their introductory promotion to either step up or full price as well as a one-month benefit from price increases on 500,000 of our more tenured full price subscriptions. We expect that the digital news subscription price increase, which went into effect in March will begin to more significantly…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/07/new-york-times-co-nyt-q1-2020-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q1","e":"nyt","d":"2020-05-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"We expect that the digital news subscription price increase, which went into effect in March will begin to more significantly benefit ARPU in the second quarter, but will be more than offset by the impact of continued strength in subscription additions, largely at the dollar-per-week promotion as…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/07/new-york-times-co-nyt-q1-2020-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q2","e":"nyt","d":"2020-08-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Meredith Kopit Levien","x":"In the quarter, digital subscription revenue grew by 30%, driven by the rapid growth in subscription additions, promotional subscriptions graduating to higher prices and the benefit we saw from our digital price increase.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/05/new-york-times-co-nyt-q2-2020-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q2","e":"nyt","d":"2020-08-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"…and have graduated to higher prices and the impact from our first ever digital subscription price increase, which began late in the first quarter. Quarterly digital news subscription ARPU declined approximately 11% compared to the prior year and approximately 3% compared to the prior…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/05/new-york-times-co-nyt-q2-2020-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q2","e":"nyt","d":"2020-08-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"We recorded a $6 million severance expense in the quarter, largely as a result of workforce reductions, primarily affecting our advertising department.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/05/new-york-times-co-nyt-q2-2020-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q2","e":"nyt","d":"2020-08-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark Thompson","x":"So we've been able -- a move we had -- in the first couple of years, we had some buyouts and layoffs and we've had some since, which have been about organizational change in shifts, which new leadership themselves have wanted to make to pivot to their new strategy.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/05/new-york-times-co-nyt-q2-2020-earnings-call-transc.aspx"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q3","e":"nyt","d":"2020-11-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"…to higher prices; and finally, the positive impact from our first-ever digital subscription price increase, which began late in the first quarter. Digital news subscription ARPU for the quarter declined approximately 11% compared with the prior year and approximately 3% compared to the…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/05/new-york-times-co-nyt-q3-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q3","e":"nyt","d":"2020-11-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"…dollar per week promotion domestically and our deeper promotional rates in many areas outside of the U.S. continue to more than offset the benefits from both subscriptions graduating from their introductory promotion as well as from price increases on our more tenured full price subscriptions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/05/new-york-times-co-nyt-q3-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2021-02-04","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Meredith Kopit Levien","x":"The Times sold its first digital subscription 10 years ago this quarter reflecting back these last 10 years have been all about proving out our strategy of journalism we're paying for through direct to consumer digital subscription.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/04/new-york-times-co-nyt-q4-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2021-02-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Meredith Kopit Levien","x":"…and Games broke all previous records for annual net ads, and we saw continued success with our two strategic pricing initiatives in News, stepping up promotional subscriptions to higher prices at the one-year mark and nearly a full year of our first-ever price increase on tenured subscription.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/04/new-york-times-co-nyt-q4-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2021-02-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Meredith Kopit Levien","x":"…fluctuations in the new cycle that could drive variability in net adds from quarter to quarter, but with every passing quarter, there is also more in our control, from an improving understanding of consumers to pricing power to more disciplined management of cost in our legacy business.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/04/new-york-times-co-nyt-q4-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"NYT 2020 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2021-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Thomas Yeh","x":"…on the expense base, maybe on the print side, we saw some rationalization of that cost structure last year, with the circulation declining around COVID, is this an area where we might see some more restructuring this year or are some expense kind of coming back as things stabilize a bit more?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/04/new-york-times-co-nyt-q4-2020-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"NYT 2021 Q1","e":"nyt","d":"2021-05-05","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Meredith Kopit Levien","x":"And the main idea here would be mainly scaling our direct-to-consumer digital subscription business.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/05/new-york-times-co-nyt-q1-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"NYT 2021 Q1","e":"nyt","d":"2021-05-05","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Meredith Kopit Levien","x":"We have a really clear strategy that we are in the business of scaling our direct-to-consumer digital subscriptions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/05/new-york-times-co-nyt-q1-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"NYT 2021 Q1","e":"nyt","d":"2021-05-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"…new subscriptions we have added in the past year; second, ongoing strength in retention of the $1 per week promotional subscriptions, who have graduated to higher prices; and finally, the positive impact from our digital subscription price increase, which began late in the first quarter of 2020.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/05/new-york-times-co-nyt-q1-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"NYT 2021 Q1","e":"nyt","d":"2021-05-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"This improvement was primarily a result of subscriptions graduating from their introductory price to either full-price or an intermediate step-up in the quarter, as well as the continued benefit from price increases on our more tenured full-price subscriptions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/05/new-york-times-co-nyt-q1-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"NYT 2021 Q2","e":"nyt","d":"2021-08-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"…number of new subscriptions we have added in the past year, continued strength and retention of the $1 per week promotional subscriptions who graduated to higher prices, and finally, the positive impact from our digital subscription price increase, which began late in the first quarter of 2020.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/04/the-new-york-times-company-nyt-q2-2021-earnings-ca/"},{"c":"NYT 2021 Q2","e":"nyt","d":"2021-08-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"This improvement was primarily a result of subscriptions graduating from their introductory price to either a full price or an intermediate step up price in the quarter as well as the continued benefit from price increases on our more tenured full price subscriptions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/04/the-new-york-times-company-nyt-q2-2021-earnings-ca/"},{"c":"NYT 2021 Q2","e":"nyt","d":"2021-08-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Roland A. Caputo","x":"And when you control for severance and multiemployer pension withdrawal obligation costs, G&A costs would have increased by 19%, largely due to increased head count in support of employee growth in other areas, higher outside services and a higher incentive compensation accrual.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/04/the-new-york-times-company-nyt-q2-2021-earnings-ca/"},{"c":"NYT 2021 Q3","e":"nyt","d":"2021-11-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland Caputo","x":"…grew as a result of the large number of new subscriptions we have added in the past year, continued strength in retention of the $1 dollar-per-week promotional subscriptions who have graduated to higher prices, and to a much lesser extent, the impact from our digital subscription price increase.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/03/the-new-york-times-company-nyt-q3-2021-earnings-ca/"},{"c":"NYT 2021 Q3","e":"nyt","d":"2021-11-03","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Roland Caputo","x":"…in both the year-over-year and sequential result was primarily due to subscriptions graduating from their introductory price to either full price or an intermediate step-up price in the quarter, as well as the continued benefit from price increases on our more tenured, full-price subscriptions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/03/the-new-york-times-company-nyt-q3-2021-earnings-ca/"},{"c":"NYT 2025 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2026-02-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Will Bardeen","x":"Total digital-only ARPU grew year over year to $9.72 as we stepped up subscribers from promotional to higher prices and raised prices on certain tenured subscribers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/ny-times-nyt-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"NYT 2025 Q4","e":"nyt","d":"2026-02-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Will Bardeen","x":"And then the timing of targeted price increases can play a role as well.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/04/ny-times-nyt-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"NYT 2026 Q1","e":"nyt","d":"2026-05-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William Bardeen","x":"So now as it relates to that sort of the drivers there, ARPU was driven specifically by subscribers transitioning from promotional to higher prices and the impact of some price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/06/nyt-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"NYT 2026 Q1","e":"nyt","d":"2026-05-06","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"William Bardeen","x":"I mentioned that a bundled price increase on the last call.","url":"https://w